prompt:
Use Three.js to implement a 3D anatomy model explorer. Load the ScatteringSkull.glb model, allow users to toggle the visibility of different parts using buttons, highlight a part and display its name when clicked, and provide adjustable opacity.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import via ES Modules in <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { GLTFLoader } from 'three/addons/loaders/GLTFLoader.js';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Model Loading]
(1) Use GLTFLoader to load assets/ScatteringSkull.glb;
(2) After loading is complete, traverse all child meshes in the model and record the list of names;
(3) Center the model at the scene origin;

[OrbitControls]
(4) Support rotation and zooming for viewing, with minDistance=0.5, maxDistance=5;

[Part Visibility Controls]
(5) Create a toggle button (DOM button) for each major child mesh in the model and place it in the left panel (id="partsList");
(6) Clicking a button toggles the visible property of the corresponding mesh;
(7) The button displays the part name and turns gray when the part is hidden;

[Part Selection Highlighting]
(8) Use Raycaster to detect mouse clicks on meshes;
(9) Set the selected mesh's emissive color to blue (0x4488ff), and restore the original materials of all other meshes;
(10) Display the selected part name in the right panel (id="detailPanel");

[Opacity Control]
(11) Provide a global opacity slider (id="opacitySlider", range 0.1-1.0, step 0.05);
(12) Adjusting the slider changes the opacity of all visible meshes;

[HUD Display]
(13) HUD in the upper-left corner:
  - Number of visible parts (id="visibleCount")
  - Selected part name (id="selectedPart"; display "None" when nothing is selected)
  - Current opacity (id="opacityValue")

[State Exposure (Required)]
Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame:
  - modelLoaded: boolean
  - totalParts: number (total number of parts)
  - visibleParts: number (number of visible parts)
  - selectedPart: string (selected part name; "" means none)
  - opacity: number (current opacity)
  - cameraDistance: number

Output a standalone HTML file in the same directory as assets/, and run it through an HTTP server.
